A mutual fund scheme shall not invest:  
i. more than 10% of its NAV in InvIT units overall;  
ii. more than 5% of its NAV in InvIT units issued by a single issuer.

The regulatory obligation regarding the use of Artificial Intelligence tools by investment advisers was first introduced through the SEBI (Investment Advisers) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2024, effective from 16-12-2024.  

It requires that an investment adviser using AI tools, irrespective of scale or adoption scenario, shall be solely responsible for:  
1. The security, confidentiality, and integrity of client data;  
2. The use of any other information or data to arrive at investment advice;  
3. Investment advice based on the output of AI tools;  
4. Compliance with any applicable law.

